type: software
title: "When the Simulator Forgives Losses: Reinforcement-Learning Trading Agents Learn to Gamble for Resurrection in Electricity Balancing Markets"
authors:
  - alias: gepapak
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - limited liability
  - gambling for resurrection
  - simulation-based evaluation
  - reward misspecification
  - electricity markets
  - imbalance settlement
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipelines, internal pre-registrations and aggregated results for a study of how a common simulator
  accounting convention, flooring an account's cash at zero, teaches reinforcement-learning trading agents to gamble
  for resurrection and makes standard evaluation report the behavior as profit. Includes the theory solvers, the
  environments and runners of eleven studies (an engine audit, an environment-design study, and liability studies B-J
  with PPO, A2C and DQN agents on Danish, Finnish and Norwegian imbalance spreads, a public simulator and realistic
  trading costs), an audit of public RL trading environments, a reconciliation tool, a placebo-market test and an
  evaluation checklist.
